Linux kernel
============

This file was moved to Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst

Please notice that there are several guides for kernel developers and users.
These guides can be rendered in a number of formats, like HTML and PDF.

In order to build the documentation, use ``make htmldocs`` or
``make pdfdocs``.

There are various text files in the Documentation/ subdirectory,
several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.
See Documentation/00-INDEX for a list of what is contained in each file.

Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.

## P22H190 cloud builds

The `Build P22H190 kernel` GitHub Actions workflow downloads Google's
official Android clang r383902 toolchain, installs the host dependencies, and
runs `scripts/build-p22h190.sh all`. A successful push to `main` or manual
workflow dispatch creates a prerelease containing:

* an AnyKernel3 flashable package with the KPM-patched kernel and modules;
* a rebuilt `socko.img` with kernel-compatible module CRCs and vermagic;
* `SHA256SUMS` and the build log as workflow artifacts.

The same build logic can be run locally after preparing the toolchain and
packaging inputs:

```sh
ANDROID_CLANG_DIR="$HOME/android-clang-r383902b/clang-r383902/bin" \
KPM_PATCHER="$HOME/kpm/patch_linux" \
ANYKERNEL_DIR="$PWD/out/AnyKernel3" \
./scripts/build-p22h190.sh all
```
